  "caption": "Quinn loves long grocery runs (the trolley helps), but a walk to the park turns both legs heavy. Sitting down eases it, and cycling feels fine.\n\nThat pattern can point to lumbar spinal stenosis: standing tall narrows the space around the lower back nerves, while bending forward opens it up.\n\nWhat often helps: walk-rest intervals instead of giving up walking, cardio with a slight forward lean (bike, water walking, incline treadmill), hip and trunk strength, and a walking pole or trolley for longer outings. Comfortable distance can improve over weeks.\n\nNew bladder or bowel changes, numbness in the saddle area or legs weakening quickly need urgent medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
